# S12.1 final review: repository writer versus acceptance race

## Scope

Source-only correction before freeze, merge and the sole server deployment.
No server state, credential, service, timer, public endpoint or deployment
attempt was touched.

## Finding

The controller rejected a conflicting sync process during preflight and
verified canonical identities after synchronization, but the credential-bearing
systemd acceptance still imported Application code from the shared canonical
worktree. A new `chatops` Git/sync writer starting after the identity check
could therefore replace source during the one permitted acceptance.

## Correction

- After canonical synchronization, install the existing atomic Git barriers
  and clone both exact reviewed repositories into a fixed root-private staging
  tree while writers remain excluded.
- Verify Application commit/tree, Control commit/tree and the annotated freeze
  target in the staged clones.
- Atomically isolate the completed stage under its root-only parent, remove all
  write bits and durably flush it before it becomes an execution source.
- Bind systemd `WorkingDirectory`, `PYTHONPATH`, Application root and Control
  root to that private tree. Keep only the pre-existing canonical virtualenv
  interpreter path; imported TU1NZ source and every release identity check use
  the immutable stage.
- On rollback, remove both fixed private release paths before writing the
  completion marker.

## Rollback plan

Revert the amended Control commit if focused tests, the complete Linux CI suite
or the next exact-SHA review is not GREEN. Do not create the freeze tag, merge
the PR or consume the single server deployment attempt.
